+---
+name: component-nexperia-bav199-215
+description: Use whenever an exact part identity, supplier code, manufacturer, pinout, package, role, source gap, or substitution for this bundle is relevant. Resolve exact Nexperia BAV199,215 evidence for its roles, pinout, package, limits, interactions and substitution review; preserve open source and physical checks.
+---
+
+# Exact component evidence owner
+
+Run `pnpm circuit:check`, read every local JSON record, and cite fact/source IDs with conditions and exact locators. Keep each record aligned with the matching inventory line and direct-routing fixture. Do not infer procurement, physical fit, system safety, or circuit qualification from a component datasheet.
+
+## Candidate status
+
+UNADOPTED S2b candidate (phase 24). It is the clamp of the `precision` variant of `high_impedance_input` (1V/OCT, MULT IN and S&H IN) and is bound to placements only inside `circuit/candidates/s2b-tmux-20261101/`; canonical adoption needs a separate approval. The record is an intentional catalogue exclusion, so no generated page exists.
+
+The retained data sheet is the JLCPCB-hosted copy of Nexperia BAV199 v.3; the nexperia.com URL was access-denied and was not worked around.
+
+## Open review points
+
+- exact orderable identity; pinout; electrical limits; manufacturer product description; mechanical fit; procurement; op-amp input overdrive remain open.
+- Stock, lead time, consignment acceptance and assembly allocation remain dated project-state gaps.
